course: dictionary
lesson: 11857
title: Bohemia: a place and a way of life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are a place name when they start with a capital letter, and a different idea when they are written in small letters. Look at the clues around the word. «We visited Bohemia on our school trip to the Czech Republic.» Here Bohemia is a place, a region with a city called Prague.
explain: Now look at small letters: «Her uncle lives in bohemia: he paints all day, plays the guitar and never wears a tie.» He does not follow ordinary rules about work or clothes. So bohemia means a free, artistic way of life.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. Does «a free, artistic way of life» make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning. If you try «a region in the Czech Republic» there, it does not fit.
fact: Bohemia is a historic region in the west of the Czech Republic.
fact: Prague is the main city of Bohemia.
fact: Bohemia was once a kingdom in central Europe, famous for glass and castles.
fact: King Wenceslas, from the Christmas carol, was a duke of Bohemia.
fact: With small letters, «bohemia» means a free, artistic way of life, led by artists, writers and musicians who do not follow ordinary rules.
exercise: «We visited Bohemia on our school trip to the Czech Republic.» In this sentence, Bohemia means: | *A region in the west of the Czech Republic | A sport played on ice | A kind of cake | A paint colour
exercise: «Her uncle lives in bohemia: he paints all day, plays the guitar and never wears a tie.» What does bohemia mean here? | A tall castle | *A free, artistic way of life | A busy office job | A loud sports club
exercise: Which city is the main city of Bohemia? | Berlin | Paris | Vienna | *Prague
test: King Wenceslas, from the Christmas carol, was a duke of Bohemia. What kind of place was Bohemia in his time? | A desert with no towns | A seaport on a busy coast | A modern airport | *A former kingdom famous for glass and castles
test: «The bohemian painters ignored the rules and slept until noon.» What does bohemian describe? | *Free-living artists who do not follow ordinary rules | Shops that open early | Strict teachers who start at dawn | Pilots who fly at night
exam: «She chose bohemia over a safe job, painting all day and sleeping late.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | *The free, artistic way of life led by artists who do not follow ordinary rules | A famous glass factory | A type of castle | A region in the Czech Republic
